note left of e_3787e043df0342c8bab7200299b751b4
Fem General 
configuration 
overview
end note

note left of ddb20b45_7347_49ef_9d0b_3f40c52bb89f
when false all 
fault events of 
this type are 
ignored.
end note

note left of ddb20b45_7347_49ef_9d0b_3f40c52bb8a3
Defines the causal
reconsideration window
for a preliminary fault.
It does not qualify
occurrence counts or
filter noisy reports.
end note

note left of ddb20b45_7347_49ef_9d0b_3f40c52bb8a4
Classifies the impact
of a confirmed fault.
end note

note left of ddb20b45_7347_49ef_9d0b_3f40c52bb8a5
Orders confirmed faults
for handling. A lower
value means higher priority.
end note

note left of ddb20b45_7347_49ef_9d0b_3f40c52bb8a6
Maps a confirmed fault
to one action: log, notify,
degrade, restart, quarantine,
or fail-safe.
end note

note left of ddb20b45_7347_49ef_9d0b_3f40c52bb8a7
Defines when and where
a confirmed fault is
escalated.
end note

note left of ddb20b45_7347_49ef_9d0b_3f40c52bb8a8
Selects time-window,
occurrence-count, or
hybrid qualification.
end note

note left of ddb20b45_7347_49ef_9d0b_3f40c52bb8a9
Sets the minimum number
of failure reports needed
to qualify a fault.
end note

note left of ddb20b45_7347_49ef_9d0b_3f40c52bb8aa
Defines the time interval
used to count failure
reports for qualification.
end note

note left of ddb20b45_7347_49ef_9d0b_3f40c52bb8a1
Configures a fault-reporting
component and its event
ownership.
end note

note left of ddb20b45_7347_49ef_9d0b_3f40c52bb8a2
When false, new fault reports
from this component are not
accepted by FEM.
end note

note left of ddb20b45_7347_49ef_9d0b_3f40c52bb8ab
Unique identifier of the
fault-reporting component.
end note

note left of ddb20b45_7347_49ef_9d0b_3f40c52bb8ac
References the optional parent
component used for causal
fault evaluation.
end note

note left of ddb20b45_7347_49ef_9d0b_3f40c52bb8ad
Defines component-level
arbitration priority. A lower
value means higher priority.
end note